---
title: 🥧 Vegetarian Chicken Pot Pie
source: Magnolia Journal
servings: 8
time: 10 hours 15 minutes
---

Combine @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}, @poultry seasoning{2%tsp}, @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} in a large #bowl{}. Add @vegetarian chicken pieces (cut into 1-inch pieces){2.5%lb}; toss to coat.

Heat @vegetable oil{1%Tbsp} in a large #skillet{} over medium-high. Add half of the vegetarian chicken; cook ~{4-5%minutes} or until browned, stirring occasionally. Transfer to a 5- to 6-qt. #slow cooker{}. Repeat with the remaining @vegetable oil{1%Tbsp} and the remaining vegetarian chicken. Deglaze pan with @vegetable broth{1/2%cup}, scraping up any browned bits; transfer to slow cooker. Add the remaining @vegetable broth{1.5%cups}, @carrots (sliced){1.5%cups}, @celery (sliced){1.5%cups}, @leeks or chopped onion (sliced){1%cup}, @cremini mushrooms (sliced){1%cup}, and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} to cooker.

Cover and cook on low ~{8-10%hours} or on high ~{4-5%hours}.

Stir in @frozen peas{1%cup}, @frozen corn{1/2%cup}, and @fresh thyme leaves{2%Tbsp}. In a bowl combine @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup} and @half-and-half{1%cup}; stir into mixture in slow cooker. If cooking on low, turn slow cooker to high. Cover and cook ~{45%minutes} more or until thickened.

Meanwhile, for biscuits, preheat oven to 450°F. In a large bowl stir together the remaining @all-purpose flour{3%cups} and @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @baking powder{1%Tbsp}, and @sugar{1%Tbsp}. Using a pastry blender, cut in @salted butter (cold, cut up){3/4%cup} until it resembles coarse crumbs. Add @buttermilk{1.25%cups}. Using a fork, stir just until mixture is moistened. Turn dough out onto a lightly floured surface. Knead dough just until it holds together. Place on a parchment paper-lined baking sheet. Pat dough into a rectangle. Cut into eight squares. Separate squares slightly. If you like, brush with additional buttermilk and sprinkle with additional pepper. Bake ~{14-16%minutes} or until golden.

Top each serving of pot pie with a biscuit. If you like, garnish with additional thyme and pepper.
